  description:
  - A blight of the skies, these opportunistic feeders consume any crop they come
    across. A noteable mutation is their hydrophilic feathers, allowing them to absorb
    water from the surrounding mist.
  - This leads to the crows having to take frequent breaks from flight, as taking
    on too much water causes their bodies to be weighed down. This can be lethal
    to the crow if it absorbed too much water mid-flight.
